[[  edit|kp format rules]]

Each ''श्लोकः'' is explained in the following format.

;Section 1:
:Original श्लोकः

;Section 2:
:पदच्छेदः (sandhi is taken away) with अन्वय  number, right subscript, in order of appearance

;Section 3:
:पदार्थथ and in sentence form

;Section 4:
:प्रतिपद व्याकर्ण विशेष 

<<<
;For nouns:

The word without sandhi = 

_-कारान्त (लिंग, पु=पुल्लिंग, स्त्री = स्त्रीलिंग, नपु = नपुंसकलिंग, त्रि = त्रिषु लिङ्गेषु)  + प्रातिपदिकम्  + the case (1 to 7)/number (1 to 3)]

विग्रह वाक्यम् if present and additional information ≡ व्युत्तपत्ति

For nouns, first digit represents the case (1 to 7) and the second digit represents
the number (1 to 3, representing singular, dual, and plural, respectively).

;For verbs:

The word without sandhi  = धातुः (root, अर्थ, कर्मणि/कर्तरि प्रयोग, प्र=प्रथम पुरुष, म=मध्यम, उ=उत्तम/ वचन १-३ )  ≡ निष्पत्ति

विग्रह वाक्यम् if present and additional information ≡ व्युत्तपत्ति


Sandhi between words shown following '}' Sandhi name (description/sutra)
<<<

;Other
(...) no special meaning | additional thought or alternative word/phrase| language translation 

:[do not include grammar/dictionary terms here]

{...} for personal use,  FUTURE: designated to be dynamically omitted 

[...] reserve for TW use. 


;Other abbreviations:

<<<
वि|वा = विग्रह वाक्यम्

वि|वि = विशेषण-वेशेष्य भाव

लि|व|वि = लिंग | वचन | विभक्ति 
<<<




